A command whose main.go writes a function only a test calls under a line
directive naming a test file. The function is written in a production file, so
it is production code only a test uses, and the test is a test of dead code.

-- go.mod --
module example.com/app

go 1.27
-- deadset.json --
{"target": {"kind": "application"}}
-- main.go --
package main

func main() {}

//line helper_test.go:3:1
func helper() {}
-- helper_test.go --
package main

// a listing long enough to hold the line main.go's directive remaps here
-- main_test.go --
package main

import "testing"

func TestHelper(t *testing.T) { helper() }
